## Training sets: name and sidecar

The SAM2 trainer consumes what `ExportTrainingData` writes. A training **set** and a trained **model** have separate
version numbers: the `3` in set `v3` is unrelated to the `3` in model `v3.1`. The model convention
(`v<VERSION>.<EPOCH>`, its `.model.json` sidecar and `description`) belongs to the trainer; the full convention is in
the Sam2Trainer repository (outside this workspace): `D:\src\git\Sam2Trainer\.cursor\rules\naming-conventions.mdc`.
In messages, logs and docstrings write "set v3", never a bare "v3".

### Naming

- A set is `v<SET>` or `v<SET>.<REVISION>`: `v2`, `v2.1`.
- `v2.1` is a repopulated or tweaked `v2` made with **the same creation rules**. Any change to the rules that define a
  sample (crop size, circle or diameter handling, filtering, ignore or approval semantics, what is exported) is a new
  set number (`v3`), never a new revision.
- A published set is immutable: re-exporting after annotation edits produces `v2.1`, not an overwritten `v2`.
- Revisions compare numerically: `v2` < `v2.1` < `v2.10` < `v3`. Do not parse a name as a float.
- `current` (the trainer's symlink) is a pointer, not a name. Record the resolved folder name.
- Names that already exist (`v1`, `v1b`, `v3`) stay as they are. Do not create new letter-suffixed names.

### The sidecar

`ExportTrainingData` writes **`training_set.json` into its `-Output` folder**, next to `manifest.jsonl`: one per volume.
The folder is later copied into the set (`SAM2TrainingData/<set>/<VOL>/`), so the sidecar travels with the volume's data.
A person never types one. The pipeline takes `-SetVersion` (`v2.1`), `-ParentSet` (needs `-SetVersion`) and
`-SetDescription`; omitted, the set named in the folder's existing sidecar is kept. Fields:

| Field | Meaning |
|-------|---------|
| `schema_version` | `1` |
| `set_version` | The set (`v2.1`); null for a folder that was never versioned. Must equal the set folder it is copied into. |
| `parent` | The set this one revises or derives from. A revision (`v2.1`) defaults to `v2`; null for a new set number. |
| `created_at`, `updated_at` | UTC, ISO 8601. `created_at` is kept while the set number stays the same. |
| `generator` | Tool and version that wrote it (`nornir-buildmanager` and its version). |
| `creation_rules` | The exporter parameters that define a sample: `pad`, `downsample`, `exporter` and its `geometry_version`, `max_texture`, `min_process_pixels`, `include_off_edge`, `channels`, `filters`, `structure_type_ids`, `odata_filter`. Not run-time settings (workers, scratch, overlays, force/update modes) and not the annotation source. |
| `creation_rules_fingerprint` | 12 hex digits of the hash of `creation_rules`. Equal for a set and its revisions, different across set numbers. |
| `source` | Where the annotations came from (`odata`, `geometries`, `viking_xml`). Informational, not a rule. |
| `description` | Free text an operator may edit. A re-export keeps what is there. |

How the exporter behaves (`training_set.py`):

- `CheckTrainingSet` is the **first** pipeline step and writes nothing: it refuses a malformed `-SetVersion`, a set number
  that would go backwards in that folder, a parent that is not an earlier set, and **changed creation rules under the
  same set number**. It runs before any section is exported, so a mistake costs seconds, not hours.
- `WriteTrainingSetInfo` is the **last** step: it writes the sidecar atomically (temp file, then replace) after the data
  it describes, so a set without one is visibly incomplete. `-Cleanup` and `-Repair` runs export nothing and leave it alone.
- A non-empty `description` is never overwritten unless `-SetDescription` is given.
- The sidecar never changes what the export builds. The only thing read back is the rules fingerprint, to enforce the
  line between a revision and a new set number.
- New rules mean a new number: `-SetVersion v3` is accepted with changed rules, `-SetVersion v2.1` is not.

